      "hints": [
        "Factorise $(3x - 1)(x - 1) = 0 \\implies \\cos^2\\theta = 1, \\frac{1}{3}$.",
        "Solve $\\cos\\theta = \\pm 1$ and $\\cos\\theta = \\pm\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ for $0^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 180^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Solve the quadratic equation in $x$ from part (i):\n$$3x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0 \\implies (3x - 1)(x - 1) = 0 \\implies x = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = \\frac{1}{3}$$",
        "Solve for $\\theta$ from $x = \\cos^2\\theta = 1$:\n$$\\cos\\theta = \\pm 1 \\implies \\theta = 0^\\circ, \\quad 180^\\circ$$",
        "Solve for $\\theta$ from $x = \\cos^2\\theta = \\frac{1}{3}$:\n$$\\cos\\theta = \\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} \\approx \\pm 0.57735$$\n$$\\theta_1 = \\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right) \\approx 54.7^\\circ$$\n$$\\theta_2 = 180^\\circ - 54.74^\\circ \\approx 125.3^\\circ$$\n$$(\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = 0^\\circ, \\quad 54.7^\\circ, \\quad 125.3^\\circ, \\quad 180^\\circ)$$"
